  "notes": "A weight-stationary systolic array fed by a weight FIFO: B shifts down through shadow weight registers for N steps and is then swapped into the active weights; a setup triangle delays row k of A by k steps, so the data enter as a diagonal wavefront; data move east and partial sums south, and below each column a rotating file of N accumulator words shares one adder. The start does not clear the PE registers; data and active weights are kept sign-extended to AccW bits. Latency 4N (16 at N = 4). The data-row vector has N(3N-1)/2*AccW bits, more than 2^31 near the top of the parameter range.",
  "player": "diagonal-heron",
